# Backend / reminders

- Stack: Python 3 + SQLite. Keep the MVP CLI (`python -m ric ...`) working.
- Store data locally in `ric/data/` (e.g. `ric.db`). Never send reminder data to cloud APIs.
- Reminder flow must work offline: create, list, trigger, confirm (`ok`), snooze (`adiar`).
- Types include at least: medicamento, consulta, tarefa (extend carefully).
- Do not couple reminder scheduling/triggers to Ollama or any LLM call.
- Prefer clear module boundaries: models/DB, scheduling, CLI. Avoid giant scripts.
- Fail safe: bad LLM output must not block or corrupt reminder state.
- Keep Windows-friendly docs/commands when touching user-facing steps.
